{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md at exact d2639ad944ed265ffac267f1d61f5dc3350cf5d2 on request/authority-r20, under promise git:sha1…883030e on request git:sha1…4ac604b\n\nAuthority, effects and publication, revision 23 at d2639ad944ed265ffac267f1d61f5dc3350cf5d2, answering the checker's changes-requested verdict 6f9cc0c7 on 55e41dfc. The facts file is unchanged. The finding: revision 22 let a further root-changing intend join an open save whose cut holds at most eight attempts, so nine could be promised a place. The repair is a bound at admission, and the join is withdrawn whole. One root-changing operation at a time: its intend opens the operation and its save in one entry, and a further root-changing intend is refused save-open while that save is open, whether or not a cut is frozen; this is the adopted recovery design's rule that mutations are serialized, now also refused at admission. A cut names every unsaved attempt or the save is refused, so no committed cut is partial and none can mark a dirty root saved or end a host. At most eight attempts are unsaved at once, which happens only when closures fail all three tries; the intend that would be the ninth is refused cut-full. A table and a short script show the count. The author's first repair kept the join with a cap; on re-reading, an intend admitted after the supervisor began the cut and before the cut's entry would have had no place in that cut, so the join was removed. A six-case table says how a waiting stop and a refused save's retry coalesce: one successor save. The recovery design is asked to carry the two refusals, the rule that a cut names every unsaved root-changing attempt, and that the supervisor starts no save job but the open one. Extents, the planner's three decisions applied: a review counts for the rules extent only from a holder of rules.publish who is independent of the authors; a single-controller exception holds only when exactly one active member with an active key holds rules.publish at the membership head the destination observes, and is recorded in the reservation entry, the publication update's reason and the receipt; it cannot be judged yet, because no observation counts the holders of an action, so until that form exists a rules-extent change needs a second controller. The obligations of the deployment and authority classes are stated for a branch landing, with which existing record carries each; for an effect beyond the branch nothing carries them, which is listed as missing. An approver is always an action a member holds. Missing forms: 13, of which 3 are answered by the planner and 10 are owed, with owners. The lane forms successor (request fdc3d7e2) is named as the place the change lane's reading is designed, with three things asked of it. Two consequences of the exception are recorded plainly in the adversarial section: two admins who disagree can each remove the other and then be sole controller, which the exception does not create and which membership's history records; and a member with no active key is not counted. Reading limits: the recovery design was read at its adopted revision 6 in two passages; its revision 9 was not read. Design only: nothing was run.","body":{"commit":"d2639ad944ed265ffac267f1d61f5dc3350cf5d2","path":"notes/2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md"}}